SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a ball that stays put at a plane and a tube of its radius is
walked with the edges beside it, and its contact with the plane, a point,
runs along no edge (mitcad#1412).

- ChFi3d_KParticular: a plane and a cylinder of the ball's radius about the
  circle they meet in, the material inside the cylinder and the edge
  convex, are no particular case: the torus would have no tube circle (the
  ball's centre stays on the cylinder's axis, its contact with the plane
  one point). The edge (between a lid's top and an earlier vertical
  rounding of the ball's radius, 0.045 mm long before the mitre where that
  rounding meets the one along the top) is walked with the mitre beside
  it, over which the ball stays put too (1520). As a particular case it
  was a sphere piece touching the top at one point, its neighbours'
  contacts taken off the top and onto the rounding along it there, and
  the top's and that rounding's faces came out broken.
- runsAlongEdgePart: a contact curve that is one point (the walked piece's
  contact on the rounding along the top, the ball staying put touching it
  at its edge with the top) runs along no part of an edge: it was taken
  for one along that edge, the piece split there and its end there given
  an external transition, and the rounding along the top lost its edge
  with the top.

The case: 1520's lid, its top rim rounded through the mitres; without
this patch the top rim's chain failed (its walked piece took the top for
its second face) or, with the sphere piece, came out invalid.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
index 07ba8dfd..8ed8e86e 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
@@ -789,6 +789,24 @@ bool ChFi3d_KParticular(const occ::handle<ChFiDS_Spine>& Spine,
     }
     else if (aCT == GeomAbs_Circle && aD1.IsParallel(aD2, aPA))
     {
+      // A cylinder of the ball's radius with the material inside it, rounded along its circle
+      // with the plane at a convex edge: the ball's centre stays on the cylinder's axis, its
+      // contact with the plane one point (mitcad#1412: the short edge between a lid's top and
+      // an earlier vertical rounding of the ball's radius, before the mitre where that rounding
+      // meets the one along the top). The torus would have no tube circle to roll on; the walk
+      // takes the edge with the ones beside it, over which the ball stays put too.
+      const gp_Cylinder aCyl     = aS2.Cylinder();
+      bool              aOutward = aCyl.Position().Direct();
+      if (aS2.Face().Orientation() == TopAbs_REVERSED)
+      {
+        aOutward = !aOutward;
+      }
+      if (!fs.IsNull() && aOutward && std::abs(aCyl.Radius() - fs->Radius(IE)) <= 1.e-6
+          && ChFi3d::DefineConnectType(Spine->Edges(IE), aS1.Face(), aS2.Face(), 1.e-5, false)
+               == ChFiDS_Convex)
+      {
+        return !bRet;
+      }
       return bRet;
     }
   }
@@ -3208,6 +3226,10 @@ static bool runsAlongEdgePart(const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>& C,
   {
     return false;
   }
+  // (A contact that is one point, a ball that stays put touching F there, mitcad#1412, runs
